{
  "format": "semio.generation3d.interaction-scope",
  "version": 1,
  "note": "What each of the six framework-reserved interaction verbs repaints in the procedural 3d editor and viewer. Nothing here is hand-written per window: the framework DERIVES the scope from the app's own declarations (`interaction_declared_refresh_scope` over `WindowKindDefinition.interactions`), and this table is what that derivation must answer. `windowBodies` is the body of every window kind that declares the `graph` domain, in declaration order; `panelBodies` is every declared panel leaf body (framework tabs included) and is empty for every verb that moves no selection, because a panel row that chased the pointer would flicker rather than inform. `publishes` names the bodies whose render consumes the interaction marks — a verb may never narrow below the ones that publish ITS lane, which is the assertion that keeps the derivation honest as windows are added.",
